To make `makemigrations --check` consistent with other management commands that use `--check` (like `migrate`), it should exit without attempting to write any migration files. Currently, `makemigrations` detects changes and then proceeds to call `write_migration_files` (or `write_to_last_migration_files`) before checking if `check_changes` is set.

If `check_changes` is True, the command should only report whether changes were detected and then exit.

The logic should be modified so that if `check_changes` is set, we only report the presence of changes (if any) and exit, without calling the write methods.

Wait, looking at the code:
```python
